<!--
  AutoAgent IL2CPP link.xml — guards against managed-code stripping.

  When a Unity project is built with the IL2CPP scripting backend, the
  managed bytecode stripper removes types and methods it cannot statically
  prove are used. The AutoAgent adapter is driven indirectly — Unity
  lifecycle hooks start it, and a WebSocket JSON-RPC loop dispatches wire
  methods at runtime — so the stripper can wrongly drop reflection / dispatch
  targets. Preserving the whole runtime assembly keeps the adapter intact in
  IL2CPP players.

  This protects the ADAPTER only. If YOUR game code relies on reflection,
  see docs/users/il2cpp-setup.md for how to add your own link.xml.

  Unity automatically picks up any .xml asset whose root element is <linker>.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="AutoAgent.Runtime" preserve="all" />
</linker>
